# Typography — one-line cards & phrase wrap

When editing copy or card/heading UI on this site, keep titles readable and consistent **everywhere** (home rails, campus cards, academics, explore, notices, events):

## Always wrap titles with `AmpersandText`
- Import from `src/components/site/AmpersandText.tsx` (`TitleText` alias is fine).
- Use it on **every** card/rail/list heading that can wrap mid-phrase — not only text that contains `&`.
- Examples fixed by the helper:
  - `Electronics & Communication Engineering` → `Electronics & Communication` / `Engineering`
  - `Medical Lab Technology Laboratory` → `Medical Lab Technology` / `Laboratory`
  - `Diploma programs & departments` → stays readable (`Diploma programs &` / `departments` or one line when space allows)
  - `Travel & Tourism` → `Travel &` / `Tourism`

## Short card subtitles
- Spotlight / unit supporting lines should stay on **one line** when possible (`whitespace-nowrap` + `truncate`).
- Prefer canonical one-line strings from `src/lib/site-data.ts` over stale CMS variants when titles match.

## Centered supporting paragraphs
- Prefer `text-pretty` on centered short blurbs so a single word (e.g. `institute.`) is not stranded on the last line.
- Widen `max-w-*` slightly or rewrite the sentence if an orphan remains.

## Ampersand rule
- Never leave `&` alone at the start of a line.

## Alignment
- In equal-height card grids, pin footer CTAs (`Discover`, `Explore`) with `mt-auto`.

## Do not skip components
If a new card/rail is added, wire `AmpersandText` on its title in the same change. Missing it on one rail (e.g. facilities) is a bug.
